cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GRANITE: General-Relativistic Adaptive N-body Integrated Tool for Extreme Astrophysics"
message: "If you use GRANITE in your research, please cite this software using the metadata in this file."
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/LiranOG/Granite-NR"
url: "https://github.com/LiranOG/Granite-NR"
version: 0.6.8
date-released: "2026-05-09"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20284043"
abstract: >-
  GRANITE is an open-source C++17 numerical relativity and General-Relativistic
  Magnetohydrodynamics (GRMHD) engine. It implements CCZ4 spacetime evolution
  with moving-puncture gauge and active constraint damping, Valencia GRMHD
  with HLLD Riemann solvers and constrained transport, fully dynamic block-
  structured Berger-Oliger adaptive mesh refinement with subcycling, an M1
  radiation transport and neutrino leakage formalism, and a complete initial-
  data solver suite (Brill-Lindquist, Bowen-York, Two-Punctures, Superposed
  Kerr-Schild). The engine targets extreme astrophysical scenarios including
  multi-body supermassive black hole mergers in dense stellar environments.
keywords:
  - numerical-relativity
  - general-relativity
  - CCZ4
  - GRMHD
  - black-holes
  - gravitational-waves
  - adaptive-mesh-refinement
  - astrophysics
  - computational-physics
  - HPC
